-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for CrossDeloop
-- (doc/delooping-direct.pdf, Section 2: (lambda0)-(lambda3), (Delta0), (Delta1)): one entry
-- per declaration, generated from --opened (28 Oct 2026) and read against the
-- note.  Kinds of openings:
--   types and levels: PtMap, PtSec, PtEquiv, Maps.PMO, the module types
--     ENat.M / N / K1 / k0;
--   by-definition steps of the text: LoopConj.conj and EH.O (conj-eh); ptcomp,
--     ptid, pt-inv / Acc.inv (the maps of composites and inverses); Evx, cx,
--     P, Q, e4i, gamma0, gamma-hat, A1, A2 (the local definitions); Inv.lam,
--     Inv.dfun, Inv.Delta (Delta-fun, before Delta is locked), ptconst and
--     sym refl / trans refl refl (delta0: Delta^0 is refl by definition); the
--     pointing of ev_x is refl, so sym refl / trans u refl compute (ev-loop:
--     Prelude.sym, trans, ap, PtMapLoops.pt0); ENat.E / Ex / phi, EDef.phi,
--     PtMapLoops.ev / ev-pt / R, FT.tr (hh: phi c ; Ex x at k is ev of loop c,
--     as ENat.hh); Maps.loop / D / Kf, idJR, trans (a looping compared through
--     Maps.D before its arguments, as ENat.e-nat; documented in s3.opens);
--   extras, not steps of the text: the chain KZ2 -> KK.K -> EMSpace.K ->
--     EMn.Kstage / stage2 -> EM2.K2 -> Deloop.Torsors.Tor opened for variables
--     over KZ2 (the etaV mechanism, doc/etav-lock-diagnostic.txt; reported on
--     the declaration after the variable); hh opens EM1.K1, TrivialGerbe.TrivG.K
--     / img when e1inv is applied, as ENat.hh (h4.opens).
